  "nativeAdaptations": [
    "No synthetic PointerEvent or browser import: pointer/key/native activation retain original event objects; point metadata uses finite native page coordinates or requests the actual public native-ref rectangle for coordinate-free activation",
    "Existing native Enter/Space capture/default-handled policy replaces browser Enter-to-synthetic-pointer dispatch. Actual key defaults, focus modality, bounds and native fidelity still require proof",
    "Current source priority state drives the real value backend; callbacks run postRender and carry attachment/window/epoch leases; original native responder negotiation and caller callbacks are preserved",
    "Held hover leave is deferred until native pointer release/cancel; reentry starts again and clears the deferral, matching the inspected pinned source",
    "Same native root/ref/editor survives interaction prop changes; no accessible grouping, editor methods/values/selection changes or SDK flag changes are introduced",
    "Pan retains the pinned 3-unit threshold, frame-coalesced/retransformed movement, 100ms recent-history velocity, stale hold-origin handling, update/postRender callback phases and original cancel-event/last-point semantics",
    "Locked RN0.86.3 defaults W3C pointer dispatch off on both platforms. Existing bubbling touch events supply native pan without responder capture or SDK flag changes; an available pointer stream and touch stream share one source-owned session without timing heuristics",
    "Native admission keys source plus actual pointerId/touch identifier. Secondary starts/foreign IDs do not retire the original session. Source comparisons cover matching physical-pointer traces; native admission/deduplication guards are separate source assertions and still require actual native proof",
    "The pan callbacks truthfully accept original native pointer or touch events. Pointer-only buttons/modifiers remain on their real event variant; no absent touch fields are fabricated",
    "Pinned RN public declarations use string touch IDs while Flow and native emitters use numbers. The owned pan event type preserves string or number IDs; admission distinguishes their types without coercion or event mutation",
    "Drag uses existing bubbling touch/available pointer events on the original owner and passive same-window scope observation for manual handles; original event objects, caller order, responder negotiation and defaults are preserved",
    "Actual native query latency retains the session history and buffers the latest move until layout is available; retired leases discard pending work. Queries never strip or temporarily write mounted styles",
    "Axis locks are owned per actual native window and always released on retirement. Global drag admission/revision prevents a tap after an intervening drag; propagated drag also cancels its own tap cycle",
    "Native public nodeName/parentElement reads identify RN:TextInput descendants. The locked native DOM implementation normalizes AndroidTextInput to that name; TextInput.State intentionally does not export its private isTextInput helper",
    "Native geometry streams and actual ref rectangle reads trigger layout/scroll compensation and constraint resize progress without resetting editor values, refs or methods",
    "Cursor snapping preserves the pinned raw event point even when configured page transforms apply to pan points and measured boxes; an actual source differential caught and corrected the initial transformed-cursor divergence"
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Full native projection/shared-layout/presence integration, including transformed ancestor coordinate fidelity and projection animation blocking",
    "Actual native touch/pointer/multitouch/manual-handle/outside-root/window/default routing, editor invariants, cancellation and held hover/drag/tap arbitration",
    "Actual constraint measurement/resize/scroll/inertia/snap/Reduce Motion/skip/frame/load fidelity on both native platforms and required profiles",
    "Global authored tap target/propagation, viewport, complete Card/public APIs, fresh consumers/products and full catalogue/profile/closure acceptance"
  ]
